{"content":[{"c":["MUTENESS"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["The inability to speak. Muteness, or aphasia, can be a momentary phenomenon or a permanent handicap. It may result from mental retardation, brain lesion, or deafness."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The Bible records several examples of muteness. Zechariah was made mute by the angel Gabriel for not believing he would become the father of John the Baptist (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.1.18-22","r":"Luke.1.18-22","rawR":"Luke.1.18-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.1.18-22","value":"Luke.1.18-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 1:18-22"},"). That condition persisted at least nine months, until the baby was born and named (vv ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.1.62-64","r":"Luke.1.62-64","rawR":"Luke.1.62-64","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.1.62-64","value":"Luke.1.62-64"}],"t":"ref","v":"62-64"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Inability to speak is usually associated with neurological diseases or severe structural deformities. When Jesus healed people who were thus afflicted, or hearing-impaired (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.9.32-33","r":"Matt.9.32-33","rawR":"Matt.9.32-33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.9.32-33","value":"Matt.9.32-33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 9:32-33"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.12.22-23","r":"Matt.12.22-23","rawR":"Matt.12.22-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.12.22-23","value":"Matt.12.22-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:22-23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.15.30-31","r":"Matt.15.30-31","rawR":"Matt.15.30-31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.15.30-31","value":"Matt.15.30-31"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:30-31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.7.32-37","r":"Mark.7.32-37","rawR":"Mark.7.32-37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.7.32-37","value":"Mark.7.32-37"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 7:32-37"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.9.17-27","r":"Mark.9.17-27","rawR":"Mark.9.17-27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.9.17-27","value":"Mark.9.17-27"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:17-27"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.11.14","r":"Luke.11.14","rawR":"Luke.11.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.11.14","value":"Luke.11.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 11:14"},"), observers were understandably astonished."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Other scattered biblical passages refer to muteness in people (",{"href":"?bref=Pr.31.8","r":"Pr.31.8","rawR":"Pr.31.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.31.8","value":"Pr.31.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 31:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.35.6","r":"Isa.35.6","rawR":"Isa.35.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.35.6","value":"Isa.35.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 35:6"},") and in animals (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.56.10","r":"Isa.56.10","rawR":"Isa.56.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.56.10","value":"Isa.56.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 56:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Pet.2.16","r":"2Pet.2.16","rawR":"2Pet.2.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Pet.2.16","value":"2Pet.2.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Pt 2:16"},"). The fact that false gods and idols cannot speak (",{"href":"?bref=Hab.2.18-20","r":"Hab.2.18-20","rawR":"Hab.2.18-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hab.2.18-20","value":"Hab.2.18-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hb 2:18-20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.12.2","r":"1Cor.12.2","rawR":"1Cor.12.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.12.2","value":"1Cor.12.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 12:2"},") was frequently pointed out by the prophets, who contrasted them with the living, speaking God of Israel."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Medicine and Medical Practice"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Muteness","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Lk 1:18-22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.1.18-22","rawQueryValue":"Luke.1.18-22","sourceRefExact":"Luke.1.18-22"},{"anchorText":"62-6